# Example CARD-DRIVEN loop (#706): watches automation cards parked on an
# upstream application bug and resumes them when that bug is fixed. STAGED /
# INERT — this is a draft for review; it does not run until renamed and its
# [DISCUSS] points (see the .md) are settled.
#
# Depends on the file-app-bug flow (#700): a blocked automation card carries the
# `blocked:app-bug` label + a `Waiting on EliteaAI/elitea_issues#N` line naming
# the upstream bug (`.agents/workflow.md` § Blocked on an app bug). This loop polls
# each such issue; when it closes, it signals the card is ready to resume.
#
# Rename to track-app-issues.env + track-app-issues.md to activate:
# ./factory/run.sh track-app-issues
AGENT="test-automation-lead"
STATUS_READY="Blocked"                 # trigger column: parked cards
QUERY="label:blocked:app-bug"          # only cards waiting on an upstream app bug
SID_SCOPE="track-app-issues"           # own conversation namespace (card-driven)
POLL="24h"                              # app fixes take days — poll a few times a day
MAX_TURNS=""
# Reads board cards + upstream issue state, writes card moves + comments. It must
# NEVER set the human-only states (Approved, Done) — see the .md guardrail.
# EXCLUSIVE not needed: no git working-tree writes.
